0..73 Comment "//! A row may name an instance of an interface by a label: `say` performs"
74..153 Comment "//! `std.io.Console.Eff` through its instance `out`, apart from the interface\'s"
154..234 Comment "//! default and from every other instance, so one row holds two instances of one"
235..311 Comment "//! interface. The label is a parameter the function abstracts, placed after"
312..392 Comment "//! every parameter it writes: a call supplies it by name, `say[.out = c]()`, or"
393..473 Comment "//! omits it and passes the one instance of the interface handled where the call"
474..552 Comment "//! stands, a capability scope\'s capability or a label of the caller\'s own row"
553..620 Comment "//! [Brachthauser-2020-effects_as_capabilities]. What refuses is in"
621..676 Comment "//! `../../pathological/control/named-instances.gandr`."
677..680 Comment "//!"
681..697 Comment "//! - see: #2271"
698..754 Comment "//! - cites: [Brachthauser-2020-effects_as_capabilities]"
755..758 Comment "//!"
